The Vulkan backend's memory: a device whose device-local memory is all
host-visible has no "invisible heap", and findMemoryTypeIndex then found no
memory for FidelityFX's device-local resources, so every FSR 3 context failed
at its first resource (FFX_ERROR_BACKEND_API_ERROR from ffxCreateContext).
A CPU renderer (lavapipe: one memory type, device-local and host-visible)
is one, as is an integrated GPU whose driver offers no device-local memory
that the host cannot see. With this change such a device's device-local
memory is taken when no other is there; every other device chooses as
before.

A change to AMD FidelityFX SDK v2.4.0's Kits/FidelityFX/backend/vk/ffx_vk.cpp
(MIT, Copyright (C) Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; the SDK's
Kits/FidelityFX/docs/license.md). This change: Copyright (c) 2026 the bbhost
authors, under the same MIT terms. Applied by tools/fetch_fidelityfx.sh.

--- a/Kits/FidelityFX/backend/vk/ffx_vk.cpp
+++ b/Kits/FidelityFX/backend/vk/ffx_vk.cpp
@@ -408,6 +408,17 @@
         }
     }
 
+    // A device whose device-local memory is all host-visible (an integrated GPU, a CPU renderer) has no invisible heap:
+    // its device-local memory then.
+    if (bestCandidate == UINT32_MAX && requestedProperties == VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_DEVICE_LOCAL_BIT) {
+        for (uint32_t i = 0; i < memProperties.memoryTypeCount; i++) {
+            if ((memRequirements.memoryTypeBits & (1 << i)) && (memProperties.memoryTypes[i].propertyFlags & requestedProperties)) {
+                outProperties = memProperties.memoryTypes[i].propertyFlags;
+                return i;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     return bestCandidate;
 }
 
